@@ -1624,3 +1624,37 @@ Facade control-flood repeats must not send a full wake train before every succes
 - 2026-09-02: A pristine linked-worktree Zephyr rebuild selected system Python unless the project venv led `PATH`, and CMake 4.4 then rejected the SDK finder when the toolchain variable was absent; invoke west with `--no-sysbuild`, put the project venv first on `PATH`, and export the repository's Zephyr SDK/toolchain variables explicitly.
 - 2026-09-02: The survey HIL verifier merged a replayed abandoned generation's expected partial flag into the next successful survey even though the production GUI correctly rejected the stale packets; apply the GUI's accepted-generation gate before recording qualification evidence.
 - 2026-09-02: Some anchor evidence captures produced a truncated first typed stack sample when the next low-duty scan began before startup sampling finished, so the strict verifier rejected the transcript despite later complete samples; keep this as a failed capture rather than weakening the verifier, and investigate the sampler overlap separately.
+- 2026-09-02: A gateway-bound report whose EVENT_PROPOSE/ACCEPT negotiation exhausted could clear the proposal without charging its selected parent, while a later same-epoch Here-I-Am also erased that parent's failure quarantine; terminal contact exhaustion now holds down the exact parent and selects a remembered alternate before discovery, and passive route advertisements preserve failure and hold-down state until actual delivery success.
+- 2026-09-02: One chained `git diff --check` plus large diff/status inspection exited with a transient bus error while the same commands passed separately; split high-output Git inspection from the whitespace gate when this recurs.
+- 2026-09-02: When two click reports simultaneously used one participating relay, the relay's bounded event slots could leave one child without an ACCEPT, while async terminal accounting lost the original report identity and could restart the same-parent budget; retain the gateway-bound packet key across EVENT_PROPOSE retries, count each completed no-ACCEPT cycle once, retry the remembered parent three times, then hold it down and prefer a cached alternate before discovery.
+- 2026-09-02: The production retained-idle clicker scheduled a watchdog timer and a system-progress work item every second despite already waking for its ten-second battery LED pulse; service both watchdog progress and feed at the LED-on wake, skip the clicker-only one-second owners, and keep the battery period build-time-bounded below the hardware timeout.
+- 2026-09-02: EVENT_ACCEPT had its own six-second local-send retry owner, forcing a proposer to listen for seven seconds while shared-parent capacity rejection produced the same silence; make ACCEPT one-shot, let the retained requester own the only retry loop, use a 250 ms reply window, and retry after the 1,200 ms healthy-link release point plus bounded node-specific jitter.
+- 2026-09-02: Correction to the earlier same-epoch route quarantine: anchors can move, so every later validated Here-I-Am sequence is fresh physical evidence that clears the observed parent's failures and hold-down even within the same gateway epoch; only an exact duplicate sequence is stale.
+- 2026-09-02: The fresh-Here-I-Am contract and native regression were added while `mesh_relay_note_flood_parent_candidate` still restored the old failure count and 60-second hold-down after upsert, so refreshed real-hop anchors could enter exponentially backed-off discovery and deliver minutes late; let the validated upsert clear that stale quarantine and keep preservation only for ordinary gateway-control reverse hints.
+- 2026-09-02: A partially delivered enumeration-aware Here-I-Am left anchors in extended-PHR continuous Channel-5 receive for the long assignment budget, where standard-PHR click wakes produced only activity/CRC recovery and the clicker discovered zero anchors; every long incompatible-PHR owner must use a bounded standard-wake probe and an exact click-preemption handoff while retaining an immutable self-stop.
+- 2026-09-02: Survey first-RF ambiguity could replace the advertised remote self-stop with a shorter local window while cleanup ABORT admission/rearm failures were logged without retry, leaving reached anchors owned for minutes; retain the conservative remote bound, retry terminal cleanup boundedly, and make hard work/rearm failure release exact ownership.
+- 2026-09-02: A BLE disconnect during an acknowledged command write was correctly treated as ambiguous, but gateway ingress assigned a new admission identity to an exact host replay, so safe reconnect/resend could rerun the operation or return BUSY while the first remained active; add bounded RAM idempotence keyed by the host envelope plus semantic digest before enabling exact resend.
+- 2026-09-02: Running a bash-style loop through `script -c` selected the user's fish shell and failed before the BLE stress test; wrap scripted compound commands in an explicit `bash -lc` when their syntax is shell-specific.
+- 2026-09-02: Executing `tools/gateway_gui/ble_smoke.py` directly failed its relative imports even though the package was valid; invoke it as `.venv/bin/python -m tools.gateway_gui.ble_smoke`.
+- 2026-09-02: The Channel-9 ACK table retained only two peers and retried an unsendable ACK batch forever, so two failed reporters could reject a third even though click discovery and ranging support four anchors; size the table from the four-anchor production capacity, expire failed ACK custody by attempts and time, and let callers retire custody only after queue admission succeeds.
+- 2026-09-02: Deferred Channel-5 flood records and the complete future Here-I-Am relay burst were treated as active radio ownership, suppressing low-duty click scans for seconds before any RF was due; only physically due or active work may block the scanner, and every failed reschedule must retire or fail-stop its exact owner.
+- 2026-09-02: Enumeration prearm replaced its advertised 51,470 ms self-stop with the full operation budget before receiving a matching CLAIM, so a missing CLAIM could leave extended-PHR receive active for 30 minutes; preserve the short immutable prearm deadline and promote ownership only on validated CLAIM.
+- 2026-09-02: Survey-owned extended-PHR receive and ranging paths could hold the radio for tens of seconds to 30 minutes and explicitly discard a decoded standard-PHR click; probe within the repeated click train, terminate the exact survey owner without extending its deadline, then hand the captured click to normal processing.
+- 2026-09-02: A standalone ten-entry BLE command replay registry reduced the gateway image to 608 bytes of free RAM before it even provided complete idempotence; reuse the existing five result-custody credits for replay identity and terminal retention instead of adding a second state pool.
+- 2026-09-02: Correction to the ACK-capacity entry above: the two ACK peer slots model the relay's one upstream and one downstream connection direction, not a two-anchor click limit; keep that protocol capacity at two and fix only false custody transfer, unbounded failure ownership, or broken serialization within the existing connection model.
+- 2026-09-02: A direct-gateway retransmit that physically sent its payload but missed the short synchronous ACK slice was reclassified as an RF-send failure, erasing the relay core's two-second ACK owner and producing unbounded sub-second report retransmissions; preserve the exact live core owner, arm the remaining ACK RX window, and let normal gateway failure accounting reach bounded backoff and repair.
+- 2026-09-02: The Channel-9 ACK table had only two peer slots and no failure lifetime, so two unsendable ACKs could reject a third or fourth click reporter forever while gateway host delivery falsely recorded failed queue admission as an ACK handoff; size custody from the four-anchor click contract, expire failed owners by attempts and age, and commit handoff only after successful table admission.
+- 2026-09-02: Correction to the immediately preceding ACK-capacity entry: two Channel-9 ACK slots are the intentional one-upstream/one-downstream connection contract and must not scale with clicker ranging capacity; retain two slots, bound failed-owner lifetime, and make queue handoff reflect actual admission.
+- 2026-09-02: Enumeration CLAIM began continuous receive before binding and parsing its hop/start lane, so bind, ACK-resume, malformed-TLV, or lane-schedule failures could leave the anchor listening until the long operation deadline; roll back the exact unbound or bound CLAIM identity on every post-begin failure.
+- 2026-09-02: A gateway priority-submit failure could cancel only the lifecycle entry while leaving its FIFO tombstone with no dispatcher, and a failed retry-work reschedule could claim a phantom owner; every terminal failure must publish the next FIFO kick or retire the exact generation immediately.
+- 2026-09-02: Gateway command retries could overwrite a prepared result identity and later try to commit the original host envelope, leaking the sole reservation until all five result credits were exhausted; make the first prepared identity immutable and resolve it before every terminal conversion.
+- 2026-09-02: A delayed gateway-priority worker cleared the shared level-triggered abort after a successor generation requested the same bit, erasing the successor's preemption; clear each generation synchronously under the arbiter handoff lock before successor admission and never from delayed workers.
+- 2026-09-02: A failed gateway control-sequence maintenance reschedule left no refill owner while protected sequence runway drained to zero; keep the scheduled flag false on failure and let subsequent sequence/admission calls recreate the bounded maintenance owner.
+- 2026-09-02: Correction to the standalone replay-registry entry: the unsafe second pool was removed entirely, but RAM-safe exact BLE command replay is still unimplemented and reconnect code must not resend an ambiguous command as though idempotence existed.
+- 2026-09-02: Successful assignment keeps the gateway RF-operation singleton until BLE publication is receipted, so an absent host can block later RF commands after TABLE is already durable; split durable publisher custody from radio-operation ownership before calling this path fully live.
+- 2026-09-02: Gateway enumeration receive-start failure and a partially transmitted Here-I-Am can clear only local prearm state without proving downstream ABORT propagation, so reached anchors rely on their bounded self-stop; add identity-bound downstream cleanup without extending that self-stop.
+- 2026-09-02: A pending gateway ACK_CONFIRM barrier uses the one-hour maximum command budget and blocks the FIFO head even when later commands target unrelated anchors; bind the barrier to the exact confirmation owner's retry horizon and allow independent destinations to progress.
+- 2026-09-02: Gateway observability can overflow a terminal backlog and later replay stale progress, so terminal publication needs capacity-safe custody or explicit fail-stop before the active command owner retires.
+- 2026-09-02: The production gateway image links at 127,584 of 131,072 RAM bytes, leaving 3,488 bytes and missing the stated 4 KiB deployment reserve even after the rejected replay table was removed; recover static RAM before treating the gateway image as deployment-qualified.
+- 2026-09-02: A completed durable assignment tied its RF singleton to eventual BLE receipt, ignored two gateway receive-start failures, and could retain stale progress after terminal observability overflow; transfer the exact result and publisher terminal into existing custody before releasing RF, clean up only the matching failed listener owner, and clear stale snapshots while entering watchdog fail-stop on terminal-capacity exhaustion.
+- 2026-09-02: A live F2F1D qualification reported Here-I-Am `progress_count=3` but collected one claim because that counter means three gateway-local flood copies, not three anchor replies, and the first F1-to-direct aggregate was lost; distinguish local flood completion from the F2-to-F1-to-direct merge chain, whose immediate retry then qualified all three exact hops.
